living conditions were already  challenging in this camp for displaced  Yemenis now severe flooding has made it  worse more than 1,500 makeshift homes  have been destroyed in a Kadesh camp one  of many affected in haja province  displaced families are now trying to  rebuild their straw homes with whatever  they can find like many families here  fatima lost all she had when she was  displaced now everything has gone again  as a widow she says her family now  depends on this breadmaker  we need help organizations have come in  but they've just taken our photograph  and registered our names we don't have  anything the United Nations estimates  the floods have affected more than  80,000 people in recent months leaving  many in need of food shelter and  sanitation we've been suffering here for  more than seven months from rains  windstorm and diseases the houses here  are all destroyed some organizations  have tried to rebuild homes but they  leave them with no roofs or cover people  have died but many aid organizations are  spread thin fighting between Houthis and  allies of Yemen's internationally  recognized government pushed the country  to the brink of famine and that was  before the flooding I used to have  little bit of cooking flour but the  floods washed it all away we don't have  anything to eat everything was flooded  may God have mercy on us on our children  people living in these camps have little  support and nowhere to go they can only  hope that help come soon  Kotsay a little piece of a yawn  al-jazeera
 

